chologist Ashley Mason of the University of California, San Francisco, was drawn into the field by those findings. She noticed an intriguing pattern: people with depression tend to have difficulty with thermoregulation. \"What we know from a bunch of literature is that depressed people seem to run hot,\" she said. Her lab has tracked body temperature against depressive symptoms in wearable-device data from close to 20,000 people, finding that worse symptoms correlated with higher skin temperature and less daily temperature fluctuation.","Heating the body may function like a \"thermoregulatory workout,\" Mason says — training the system to cool down more efficiently afterward. She has run two small pilot trials combining eight weeks of cognitive behavioral therapy with four sessions in an infrared hyperthermia machine; in both studies, most participants were in remission from depression by the end. Her team is now running the same protocol in a larger pool of patients at UCSF, Harvard and the Cleveland Clinic, funded by the National Institutes of Health and others.","## Early days","Scientists are careful to temper expectations. The evidence base largely rests on animal studies, cell models and a small number of human trials, most without strict control groups. Mason stresses that the pilot results are preliminary — the studies were not powered to show the treatments were effective — but they lay the groundwork for the larger, well-controlled trials that could.","\"Heat does seem to be a promising therapy, but we're very much at the beginning of this research,\" she said. If future studies confirm the effect, heat therapy could earn a place alongside other non-pharmacological approaches for mental health, like exercise — \"a seat at the table\" for people whose depression has resisted other treatments, as Mason put it."],"category":"Health","tags":["Mental Health","Depression","Sauna","NPR","Science"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-sauna-mental-health-0-0-21af18cd-d994-43b4-b6b8-8cf0c0d7285f.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a wooden sauna interior with heat waves, a thermometer, moon and heart icons","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"NPR — 'From floating saunas to clinical trials: How heat might help mental health' (Siv Dolmen, 2026-10-05)","url":"https://kvcr.org/news/npr-top-stories/2026-10-05/sauna-heat-therapy-mental-health-depression","role":"primary"},{"name":"NPR member stations (KTTZ, WEXT, WKYU) — same reporting, independent syndication","url":"https://radio.kttz.org/2026-10-05/from-floating-saunas-to-clinical-trials-how-heat-might-help-mental-health","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"NPR (2026-10-05) reporting verified: Hilland/OsloMet 50-person RCT (Oslo harbor floating saunas), Lowry/UC Boulder mechanisms, Wisconsin 30-person trial (38.5°C, majority 50% sympt","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654791567/"},{"id":"art-0025-shelton-gea-shanghai-masters-2026","slug":"ben-shelton-arthur-gea-shanghai-masters-upset-2026","headline":"\"I Got Outplayed\": Ben Shelton Falls to France's Arthur Gea in Shanghai Masters Upset","socialHeadline":"World No. 4 Ben Shelton was stunned 7-6(5), 7-6(3) by 21-year-old Arthur Gea in the third round of the Shanghai Masters — the Frenchman's first win over a top-10 player","summary":"US Open finalist Ben Shelton was knocked out of the Shanghai Masters on Sunday, losing 7-6(5), 7-6(3) to France's Arthur Gea in the third round. The world No. 56 claimed the biggest win of his career, while Shelton admitted he had been outplayed.","body":["Ben Shelton's Shanghai Masters campaign ended in the third round on Sunday as the world No. 4 fell 7-6(5), 7-6(3) to France's Arthur Gea, according to Reuters. It was the 21-year-old Frenchman's first victory over a top-10 player and one of the biggest upsets of the 2026 season.","Both sets were decided in tiebreaks. Shelton, whose powerful left-handed serve is usually his biggest weapon, managed just 63% of points behind his first delivery as Gea's disciplined returning kept him under constant pressure. The American faced three match points at 6-3 in the second-set tiebreaker; Gea converted the first.","## Shelton's honest assessment","Shelton was candid after the defeat. \"I mean, I got outplayed today. The guy played better than me,\" he told reporters, according to Reuters. He pointed to his lack of preparation since September's US Open final, where he lost to Alexander Zverev: \"A hundred percent, I would have liked to have come over here earlier and be prepared and have already dealt with the jet lag by the time I was playing here in the Shanghai Masters.\"","The 24-year-old has barely played since New York, withdrawing from the Japan Open in Tokyo over fitness concerns. \"My body wasn't ready. I wasn't physically ready to play in Tokyo. That's just the way this tour is sometimes,\" he said.","Shelton, who won his first match in Shanghai on his 24th birthday, now turns his focus to the season-ending ATP Finals in Turin next month. \"Obviously I want to be prepared and playing some of my best tennis when I get there,\" he added. \"Three tournaments left to finish the year, which has been a very up and down year, but a great year, on a high note.\"","## A breakthrough for Gea","Gea, ranked 56th in the world, was delighted with a result he called special. \"I'm practicing hard every day since the beginning of the year to win against those guys,\" he said. \"Of course, when you win, it is always special. But, yeah, I was prepared and I was confident before the match.\"","The Frenchman now faces either Jakub Mensik or Francisco Cerundolo for a place in the quarter-finals.","Elsewhere on Sunday, 26th seed Karen Khachanov beat Adrian Mannarino 6-2, 6-4, while top seed and US Open champion Alexander Zverev was scheduled for a night match against Quentin Halys. No. 1-ranked Jannik Sinner withdrew from Shanghai earlier in the week, announcing he is taking the rest of 2026 off because of a right knee injury, the Associated Press reported."],"category":"Sports","tags":["Tennis","ATP","Shanghai Masters","Ben Shelton","Arthur Gea"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-shelton-shanghai-upset-0-0-c7c3c6b4-0006-4a48-aa56-e6e2df9bce09.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a tennis court with a racket, ball and scoreboard showing two 7-6 sets","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Gea sends Shelton crashing out of Shanghai' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/tennis/gea-sends-shelton-crashing-out-shanghai-2026-10-11/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Associated Press, via Sportsnet — 'Shelton beaten by Gea in Shanghai Masters R3' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.sportsnet.ca/atp/article/ben-shelton-ousted-in-third-round-of-shanghai-masters/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Reuters (2026-10-11) verified: 7-6(5), 7-6(3), third round, Shanghai, Sunday; world No","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0026-super-el-nino-2026-record-2026","slug":"super-el-nino-2026-record-climate-warming-2026","headline":"Scientists Track a Potentially Record 'Super El Niño' as a Warming World Fuels the Extremes","socialHeadline":"The 2026 El Niño is tracking hotter than the great events of 1997 and 2015 at the same point in the year — and scientists say it could push global temperatures to new records","summary":"The El Niño building across the Pacific in 2026 is on track to be one of the strongest ever recorded, climate scientists say, with ocean temperatures already running hotter than the famous super El Niños of 1997 and 2015. Researchers warn it could drive record global heat in 2026 and 2027, amplified by the background of human-caused warming.","body":["The warming of the equatorial Pacific known as El Niño is developing into something extraordinary in 2026, and scientists are warning that it could shatter records. Analyses of ocean temperatures suggest the event is already tracking above the great El Niños of 1997 and 2015 at the same point in their development.","\"No El Niño in the modern record has run this warm this early in its development,\" Berkeley Earth climate scientist Zeke Hausfather and chief scientist Robert Rohde wrote in a July 2026 temperature update. They estimate sea surface temperatures at the event's peak in December could run roughly 4°C above average in the key Niño regions — \"blowing the previous record out of the water.\"","## What the agencies say","The UK Met Office has called the developing event \"unprecedented,\" with its long-range GloSea forecast system showing sea surface temperatures in the Niño 3.4 region exceeding 3°C above normal in the coming months. Professor Adam Scaife, the Met Office's head of long-range forecasting, said he had \"never seen an El Niño signal this intense in our forecasts.\"","The World Meteorological Organization has warned the phenomenon will last until at least February, with severe consequences for weather worldwide, according to Wired's September reporting.","## Why it matters","El Niños are a natural part of the climate cycle, but they now play out against a planet already warmed by greenhouse gases — and that makes them more destructive. The Met Office notes that the Indian summer monsoon is already running well below normal rainfall, with Central America, western Pacific nations and tropical South America also at risk of low rainfall. El Niño also tends to suppress Atlantic hurricanes by increasing wind shear; consistent with that pattern, there have been only three Atlantic storms so far this season, though the agency cautions that a single large hurricane can still cause devastation.","For global temperatures, the outlook is stark. Rohde said during a July press briefing that it was \"now more likely than not\" that the extraordinary El Niño would bring record warmth in 2026 and \"much stronger warmth\" in 2027. Some analyses suggest the global average could climb to around 1.7°C above preindustrial levels by 2027 — above the 1.5°C threshold long treated as a guardrail.","## The climate connection","That is the focus of new reporting from Wired on how the 2026 super El Niño and climate change are related: El Niño is no longer just a temporary fluctuation but a force whose variability is intensified by a warming world, compounding cascading impacts.","The warming will not last forever — Rohde expects 2028 to be cooler as the event subsides. But the background trend keeps climbing. \"Human emissions are adding a permanent El Niño worth of heat to the climate system each decade,\" Hausfather told The Washington Post. Even as El Niño's direct influence fades, the heat it borrows against the future does not fully return."],"category":"Science","tags":["Climate","El Niño","Global Warming","Weather","Berkeley Earth"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-super-el-nino-2026-0-0-94d82c5e-c06d-464f-ace4-6385095cae64.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a Pacific Ocean world map with warm red current arrows, a rising thermometer and storm clouds","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Wired — 'How the 2026 Super El Niño and Climate Change Are Related' (2026-10-11, discovery lead)","url":"https://metaviews.ca/signal/2026-09-05-070624-super-el-nino-black-sea-grain-war-food-markets/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"UK Met Office — 'An unprecedented El Niño and its implications for the weather forecast' (official press release, 2026-08-24)","url":"https://www.wired-gov.net/wg/news.nsf/articles/An+unprecedented+El+Ni%C3%B1o+and+its+implications+for+the+weather+forecast+24082026151515","role":"primary"},{"name":"Gizmodo reporting Berkeley Earth July 2026 temperature update (Hausfather, Rohde)","url":"https://gizmodo.com/super-el-nino-could-push-earths-temperature-13-years-ahead-of-the-current-warming-trend-2000798669","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Wired 2026-10-11 story (discovery lead) corroborated by: Met Office official press release (2026-08-24, 'unprecedented', Nino3.4 >3°C, Prof Scaife quote), Berkeley Earth July updat","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0027-singapore-sparkletots-20-million-2026","slug":"singapore-pcf-sparkletots-staff-training-20-million-2027","headline":"Singapore's Largest Preschool Operator to Double Teacher Training Spend to S$20 Million","socialHeadline":"PCF Sparkletots will invest S$20 million in staff development over three years from 2027 and offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools — announced at its 40th anniversary celebrations","summary":"Singapore's largest preschool operator, PCF Sparkletots, will double its investment in staff development to S$20 million over three years from 2027, the organization announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve marking its 40th anniversary.","body":["PCF Sparkletots, Singapore's largest preschool operator, will double what it spends on training its teachers to S$20 million over the next three years, the PAP Community Foundation (PCF) announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve celebrating the foundation's 40th anniversary.","The investment will begin from 2027 and goes alongside a plan to offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools from 2027 where there is demand, plus an enhanced centralized model to cut administrative work across its centres so educators can spend more time with children and teaching.","## Four decades of PCF","Deputy Prime Minister Gan Kim Yong, who attended as guest of honour, said PCF had over 40 years supported more than a million children, served some 30,000 seniors, and empowered more than 46,000 vulnerable beneficiaries.","PCF today operates close to 350 preschool centres, making it Singapore's largest preschool operator. It is also the country's third-largest senior care provider, with 11 senior care centres and nine active ageing centres.","## Why teachers matter","PCF Council of Management chairperson Josephine Teo, who is also Singapore's Minister for Digital Development and Information, said the investment reflected the outsized role teachers play in children's learning: parents entrust the operator with their children's formative years, so it must develop its teachers to help them be more effective and give every child a strong start.","The announcement fits a longer shift in Singapore's early childhood sector, where anchor operators like PCF Sparkletots have moved from simply expanding centre numbers to upgrading teacher quality and curriculum — a direction the Early Childhood Development Agency has encouraged to keep fees affordable while raising standards."],"category":"World","tags":["Singapore","Education","Preschool","PCF Sparkletots","Asia"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-sparkletots-preschool-0-0-fba64f7b-c021-42c6-bf6b-c3abbb8bcde0.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a preschool classroom with a teacher and faceless geometric children, crayons and blocks","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"The Straits Times, via Nestia — 'PCF Sparkletots to double staff development spending to $20m' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://news.nestia.com/detail_share/14191475?media_type=1","role":"primary"},{"name":"The Straits Times, via Etleboro — same announcement (2026-10-11)","url":"https://etleboro.org/g/b894799558b53d0408036a674e9ab517en/pcf-sparkletots-to-double-staff-development-spending-to-$20m-ease-teachers’-admin-workload","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Straits Times (2026-10-11) verified via two independent syndication mirrors: S$20m over 3 years from 2027, announced Oct 11 at Mandai Wildlife Reserve family day (40th anniversary)","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0028-redwoods-heat-stress-study-2026","slug":"california-redwoods-heat-stress-photosynthesis-study-2026","headline":"California's Giant Redwoods Are Getting 'Heatstroke', a New Study Finds","socialHeadline":"When temperatures spiked, the world's tallest trees slowed photosynthesis — the process that feeds them. UC Davis researchers say the findings raise alarms for the forests' future in a warming climate","summary":"California's iconic coast redwoods — the tallest trees on Earth — slow the very process that feeds them when temperatures spike, according to a new University of California, Davis study. The findings, the first to measure heat's effect on redwood photosynthesis, raise concerns about the future of the forests as heatwaves grow more intense.","body":["The world's tallest trees are struggling to stay cool. When air temperatures topped 86°F in a Mendocino County redwood forest during the summers of 2022 and 2024, some redwood leaves ran nearly 20°F hotter than the air — a sign of stress that researchers had never fully measured before.","The UC Davis study, led by PhD candidate Lily Klinek of the Plant Optics Lab in the Department of Plant Sciences and published in JGR Biogeosciences, tracked the trees over three summers. It found that under heat stress, coast redwoods slow photosynthesis — the chemical reaction that converts sunlight, water and carbon dioxide into the carbon they need to grow. \"It's as if the trees slow their 'breathing' and, as a result, their 'eating,'\" the researchers explain.","\"The leaves aren't able to cool down,\" Klinek said — which suggests they closed their stomata, the tiny pores that take in carbon dioxide, to conserve water. Follow-up lab tests at temperatures up to 110°F confirmed that photosynthesis was reduced even when the leaves had plenty of water and kept their stomata open.","## Why redwoods are vulnerable","Redwoods evolved for cool coastal conditions, with average temperatures around 59°F. They also depend on coastal fog, which acts as a natural air conditioner. As heat spikes burn off that fog, the trees lose a key source of moisture — exactly when they need it most.","The concern is greatest for redwood forests in already vulnerable central, southern and eastern parts of their range. \"We don't know what the upper temperature thresholds are for redwood photosynthesis and mortality,\" Klinek said. \"With this work, we see there's a significant impact of heat on photosynthesis and physiology. That's an important start for figuring out what parts of the redwood range are at risk.\"","There is a sliver of good news: the trees the team studied did not lose their capacity to photosynthesize after the heat passed. \"Right now the temperatures are coming back to normal in the fall and winter and letting the trees recover,\" Klinek said. \"But in five or 10 years, if temperatures are even hotter and heat waves are even more frequent, we don't really know if there would be a recovery.\"","Independent experts share the concern. UC Berkeley plant ecophysiologist Todd Dawson, who did not take part in the study, called it \"a double whammy\": \"They're running out of water and also getting this heat stress.\" He noted redwoods are adapted to a narrow band of 8 to 27°C, and that the coastal fog they rely on has declined by 30 to 40 percent.","The study's authors include Troy Magney, Jessie Au and Milagros Rodriguez-Caton of UC Davis, Mukund Palat Rao of Columbia University, Lauren Fety of The Conservation Fund and George Koch of Northern Arizona University. It was funded by the National Science Foundation and California Forestry and Fire Protection, in cooperation with The Conservation Fund."],"category":"Science","tags":["Climate","Redwoods","California","Forests","UC Davis"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-redwoods-heat-stress-0-0-e0046d25-850a-41e1-880b-61ee372de4b7.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of tall redwood trees beside a rising thermometer, a blazing sun and a magnified leaf","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"UC Davis — 'Coast Redwoods Slow Their Breathing and Eating When Temperatures Spike' (official, 2026)","url":"https://www.ucdavis.edu/climate/news/coast-redwoods-slow-their-breathing-and-eating-when-temperatures-spike","role":"primary"},{"name":"Wired — 'California's Tallest and Most Iconic Trees Are Getting Heatstroke' (2026-10-11, discovery lead)","url":"https://www.scientificinquirer.com/2026/10/06/coast-redwoods-slow-their-breathing-and-eating-when-temperatures-spike/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"Phys.org — 'Coast redwoods slow their breathing and eating when temperatures spike' (2026-09)","url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-09-coast-redwoods-temperatures-spike.html?deviceType=mobile","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"UC Davis official page verified: Klinek (PhD candidate, Plant Optics Lab) lead author, JGR Biogeosciences, first study of heat on coast redwood photosynthesis, three summers in Men","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0029-iran-shopkeepers-war-economy-2026","slug":"iran-shopkeepers-economy-war-inflation-tehran-2026","headline":"\"Going Bankrupt\": Iran's Shopkeepers Struggle as War Wrecks the Economy","socialHeadline":"At Tehran's Tajrish bazaar, customers who once bought nuts by the kilo now buy by the handful. With inflation near 90% and the currency collapsing, merchants say they are fighting for survival","summary":"At the historic Tajrish bazaar in northern Tehran, the stalls are quieter than they used to be. Shoppers who once bought nuts by the kilogram now buy a half-kilo or less, as soaring prices driven by the US-Iran war eat into sales. Across the commercial district, many merchants say they are fighting for survival.","body":["Where fragrant herbs and spices once drew crowds through the narrow paths of the Tajrish bazaar, shops now sit mostly empty, according to an AFP dispatch carried by France 24. Nasir, a 61-year-old fruit and nut seller, said customers who \"used to buy two to five kilograms\" now buy one kilogram or half. \"Prices are truly high. We all know it, and it would be a lie to say otherwise,\" he said.","The pressure comes from a war that began in February, the dispatch reports, involving US-Israeli attacks and an American blockade of Iran's ports — on top of years of sanctions that had already battered the economy.","## Numbers in freefall","Official figures cited in the dispatch paint a bleak picture. Inflation ran at nearly 90% year-on-year in September, and food prices have more than doubled since last year. Gross domestic product contracted 10.1% year-on-year between late March and late June, according to official data.","The currency has collapsed with it: the rial traded at around 2.7 million to the dollar on the unofficial market in the past week, compared with about 1.7 million before the war. The minimum monthly wage, worth around $120 a year ago, has fallen to $65.","## 'A desperate, last-ditch struggle'","Ali Nowruzi, 36, who runs a sportswear shop in the bazaar, described the squeeze from both ends: \"It is a desperate, last-ditch struggle. Manufacturers are going bankrupt, laying off staff and closing shops, and the impact inevitably reaches us.\" He now orders only a few items for display, he said, so the shelves do not look as bare as his warehouse, which lies empty for lack of demand.","\"We have absolutely no plan for the future. When people don't come to buy… it effectively spells bankruptcy for the business,\" he said, citing rising rent and utility bills. \"We just need some stability.\"","The strain reaches far beyond the bazaar. Azadeh, a 45-year-old woman currently out of work, said a kitchen cloth that cost her 22 cents a few months ago now costs $1.10 — \"prices haven't just gone up, they've truly skyrocketed,\" she said. She has stopped buying some fruits and can no longer afford holidays. Car mechanic Mojtaba Rezaei, 57, told AFP his customers had \"dropped to a tenth of what it was\" because goods now cost two or three times as much — \"I actually feel embarrassed telling prices to customers.\"","Iran's economy minister has rejected predictions of an imminent economic collapse, accusing the country's foes of trying to fuel public anxiety and drive up exchange rates, according to the dispatch.","Independent reporting backs the broader trend: Euronews interviews with Iranians describe emptied wallets and collapsing purchasing power since the war began, while financial analysis has noted real-wage pressure across the region as the conflict disrupts energy and trade flows."],"category":"World","tags":["Iran","Economy","Inflation","Middle East","AFP"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-iran-bazaar-economy-0-0-7cad5538-a19c-4b9e-bc6d-cd6f90b6ae7a.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a covered bazaar with market stalls, a rising price tag and a declining currency graph","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"AFP, via France 24 — 'Going bankrupt': Iran shopkeepers struggle as war dims demand (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.newsbeep.com/766078/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Euronews — 'The country is falling apart': Iranians tell how war emptied their wallets (2026-09)","url":"https://dailyguardian.eu/iranians-tell-euronews-how-war-emptied-their-wallets/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AFP dispatch (via France 24 RSS, mirrored NewsBeep) verified: Tajrish bazaar, Tehran; Nasir (61) nut seller; war began February (US-Israeli attacks + US blockade of ports, attribut","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654917063/"},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["Pope Leo XIV announced on Sunday that he will undergo surgery this week after doctors discovered a nodule on his lung, telling thousands gathered in St Peter's Square for the weekly Angelus that the growth was detected at what he described as a very early stage.","The 71-year-old pontiff said his doctors had recommended the operation and that he had decided to go ahead with it, asking the crowd for their prayers. The announcement, made in person from the window of the Apostolic Palace, was his first public disclosure of a health issue since his election.","Vatican spokesman Matteo Bruni confirmed that the surgery is scheduled for the first days of the week and is expected to take place at Rome's Gemelli Hospital, the facility that has treated popes for decades. Recovery is expected to take about a week, the Vatican said.","Officials stressed that the nodule is localized and was caught early. The pope, who turned 71 this year, has had no previously known health problems during his pontificate.","The announcement raises questions about the pope's upcoming travel plans, including a scheduled trip to Latin America from November 6 to 17. The Vatican has not said whether the itinerary will be affected.","The news drew immediate reaction from Catholic leaders and heads of state, with messages of support arriving from around the world within hours of the Angelus address."],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"Pope Leo XIV to Undergo Lung Surgery This Week After Nodule Found at 'Very Early Stage'","id":"art-0030-pope-leo-lung-surgery-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of St Peter's Basilica dome silhouette with a dove and a subtle medical cross motif","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-pope-leo-surgery-20261011.webp"},"pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"pope-leo-xiv-lung-surgery-nodule-gemelli-2026","socialHeadline":"Pope Leo XIV announces lung surgery this week after doctors find early-stage nodule","sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — 'Pope Leo XIV says he will undergo surgery this week' (2026-10-11)","role":"primary","url":"https://gray-wowt-prod.gtv-cdn.com/2026/10/11/pope-leo-xiv-says-he-will-undergo-surgery-heres-why/"},{"name":"NPR — 'Pope Leo XIV to undergo lung surgery this week' (2026-10-11)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.whro.org/2026-10-11/pope-leo-xiv-to-undergo-lung-surgery-this-week"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","summary":"Pope Leo XIV told crowds in St Peter's Square on Sunday that doctors found a localized nodule on his lung and advised surgery. The Vatican says the operation will take place in the coming days at Rome's Gemelli Hospital, with about a week of recovery expected.","tags":["Pope Leo XIV","Vatican","Health","Catholic Church","Rome"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Pope's own Oct 11 Angelus announcement (Vatican) verified via AP and NPR page reads: localized lung nodule at very early stage; surgery first days of the week at Rome's Gemelli Hospital; ~1 week recovery; Vatican spokesman Matteo Bruni confirmation; pope aged 71, no known prior health issues.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["At least 109 migrants, including 15 children, have died after a boat carrying about 350 people capsized off the coast of Djibouti, the International Organization for Migration said on Sunday.","The vessel went down during the night of October 8-9 near Guhere, north of the town of Obock, while sailing from Djibouti toward Yemen, according to the IOM. The agency said 109 bodies had been recovered so far: 52 men, 42 women and 15 children, nine of them girls and six boys. More than 116 people were still missing, and over 80 survivors — all Ethiopian nationals — had been pulled from the water.","IOM teams are on the ground working alongside Djiboutian authorities, and survivors are being assisted at the agency's migrant response centre in Obock. \"This is a devastating loss of life,\" the IOM's chief of mission in Djibouti, Alexandre Coissac, said. Search and rescue operations were continuing on Sunday.","The Djibouti-Yemen crossing is one of the world's busiest and most perilous migration corridors, used each year by tens of thousands of people — many from Ethiopia — attempting to reach Gulf states in search of work. Overloaded, unseaworthy boats make the journey routinely deadly; exact passenger counts often vary in the first hours after a disaster, with some outlets reporting between 305 and 350 people aboard this vessel."],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"109 Dead, Including 15 Children, After Migrant Boat Capsizes Off Djibouti, UN Agency Says","id":"art-0031-djibouti-migrant-boat-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of dark sea waves with a lifebuoy and a map pin marking Djibouti, in somber navy tones","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-djibouti-boat-tragedy-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654917174/","pinned":true,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"djibouti-migrant-boat-capsizes-109-dead-iom-2026","socialHeadline":"At least 109 migrants dead after boat capsizes off Djibouti, IOM says","sources":[{"name":"Reuters — '109 migrants, including 15 children, dead after boat off Djibouti-Yemen capsizes' (2026-10-11)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/109-migrants-including-15-children-dead-after-boat-djibouti-yemen-capsizes-un-2026-10-11/"},{"name":"BBC News — 'Children among 109 dead after boat capsizes off Djibouti, UN says' (2026-10-11)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.bbc.com/news"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Djibouti","Migration","IOM","Yemen","Ethiopia","Disaster"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Casualty figures from IOM (UN migration agency) statement quoted verbatim in Reuters: capsizing night of Oct 8-9 near Guhere, north of Obock; ~350 aboard; 109 dead (52 men, 42 women, 15 children), 116+ missing, 80+ Ethiopian survivors; IOM chief of mission Alexandre Coissac quoted; SAR continuing.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true},"summary":"At least 109 migrants dead after boat capsizes off Djibouti, IOM says"},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["The United States on Friday imposed sweeping sanctions on the International Criminal Court, targeting the tribunal as an institution in a dramatic escalation of Washington's campaign against it.","Secretary of State Marco Rubio announced the measures, saying the administration would \"ban transactions with this rogue court, cutting off their resources and crippling its ability to operate against us.\" Under the sanctions, the court's assets in US jurisdictions are blocked, and American entities have been given a six-month wind-down period to sever ties, with exemptions for telecommunications, software, pensions and transactions involving detainees.","The court in The Hague condemned the move as \"an assault on the rule of law and on the very foundations of the international legal order,\" and called on its 125 member states to defend the institution.","The announcement came just hours after former ICC judge Navi Pillay was awarded the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize — a juxtaposition that drew immediate international attention. The measures go far beyond earlier US sanctions, which had targeted 17 individual ICC judges and officials; this is the first time the court itself has been sanctioned as an entity. US allies including Britain, Canada, Denmark, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the Netherlands issued statements of regret, and UN Secretary-General António Guterres called the move a \"serious blow.\""],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"US Imposes Sweeping Sanctions on International Criminal Court; ICC Calls It 'Assault on the Rule of Law'","id":"art-0032-us-icc-sanctions-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of the scales of justice beside a document stamped with a sanctions seal","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-icc-sanctions-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654917253/","pinned":true,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"us-sanctions-international-criminal-court-rubio-2026","socialHeadline":"US unveils sweeping sanctions on the ICC — court condemns 'assault on the rule of law'","sources":[{"name":"Associated Press (via Military.com) — 'US hits International Criminal Court with sweeping sanctions' (2026-10-09)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.military.com/us-hits-international-criminal-court-with-sweeping-sanctions-as-part-of-drive-to-dismantle-tribunal"},{"name":"Human Rights Watch — 'US sanctions on ICC put global justice at risk' (2026-10-09)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/10/09/us-sanctions-on-icc-put-global-justice-at-risk"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["United States","ICC","Sanctions","Marco Rubio","International Law"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Announced Fri Oct 9, 2026 by Secretary of State Marco Rubio, verified via AP and HRW page reads: institution-wide sanctions (transaction ban, US-jurisdiction assets blocked), 6-month wind-down for US entities, exemptions for telecoms/software/pensions/detainee transactions; ICC condemned as 'assault on the rule of law'; announced hours after Navi Pillay's Nobel win; 125 member states; UK/Canada/Denmark/France/Germany/Italy/Japan/Netherlands expressed regret; Guterres called it a 'serious blow'.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["Donald Trump lashed out at Norway late on Friday after the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to South African jurist Navi Pillay, calling the committee's decision an \"indelible stain on the country of Norway.\"","Speaking at a rally in Syracuse, New York, Trump described the award as a \"disgraceful and embarrassing decision\" and said the Norwegian Nobel Committee had been \"forever discredited.\" He told the crowd he had never heard of this year's winner. In a roughly 600-word post on Truth Social, he claimed he had \"settled eight wars\" and deserved the prize himself.","The laureate, 85-year-old Navi Pillay, is a South African jurist who served as a judge of the International Criminal Court and as the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights. Accepting the honour, she quipped: \"If you clap a little bit more, I may share this prize with Trump.\"","The prize was announced on Friday morning in Oslo. Trump has campaigned openly for the Nobel Peace Prize for years, repeatedly listing conflicts he says his diplomacy helped end — claims that fact-checkers have disputed."],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"Trump Calls Nobel Committee's Decision an 'Indelible Stain' on Norway After Prize Goes to Navi Pillay","id":"art-0033-trump-norway-nobel-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a Nobel-style gold medal beside a generic speech podium, in navy and gold tones","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-trump-nobel-norway-20261011.webp"},"pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"trump-norway-nobel-peace-prize-navi-pillay-2026","socialHeadline":"Trump blasts Norway over Nobel Peace Prize after award goes to Navi Pillay","sources":[{"name":"CNN — 'Trump: Nobel Peace Prize' (2026-10-09)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/09/politics/trump-nobel-peace-prize"},{"name":"Reuters — 'Trump says Norway has indelible stain for not awarding him Nobel Peace Prize' (2026-10-09)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://wncy.com/2026/10/09/trump-says-norway-has-indelible-stain-for-not-awarding-him-nobel-peace-prize/"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Donald Trump","Nobel Peace Prize","Navi Pillay","Norway","United States"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Verified via CNN and Reuters page reads: 2026 Nobel Peace Prize announced Oct 9, 2026, winner Navi Pillay (85, South African jurist, former ICC judge, ex-UN human rights chief); Trump's remarks at Syracuse, NY rally late Oct 9 ('indelible stain on the country of Norway', 'disgraceful and embarrassing decision', committee 'forever discredited') plus ~600-word Truth Social post claiming he settled eight wars; Pillay quipped she may share the prize with Trump.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["The Pentagon said last week it plans to livestream the December 3 firing-squad execution of Nidal Hasan, the former Army psychiatrist convicted of the 2009 Fort Hood massacre — though the announcement has since been met with confusion and public doubt from within the administration itself.","Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth told podcaster Jack Posobiec, in an interview recorded aboard the USS Abraham Lincoln on October 7: \"We'll make sure that people are able to watch it, that it's public.\" A Pentagon official subsequently confirmed the execution \"will be livestreamed.\" Acting Army Secretary Adam Telle set the date for December 3 at 1 p.m. local time, and President Trump approved Hegseth's recommendation.","Hasan was convicted in 2013 of 13 counts of premeditated murder and 32 counts of attempted murder over the November 2009 shooting rampage at Fort Hood, Texas. If carried out, it would be the first US military execution in more than 60 years — and the first by firing squad since World War II.","Alonzo Lunsford, a survivor who was shot seven times in the attack, told the BBC he supports the execution by firing squad and believes survivors and victims' families should be able to watch it uncensored.","But the plan's future is uncertain. CNN reported on October 10 that Army and Pentagon officials were caught off guard by the announcement, and Vice President JD Vance publicly cast doubt on it, saying he did not know whether the livestream would actually happen."],"breaking":false,"category":"US","editorPick":false,"headline":"Pentagon Says Fort Hood Shooter's Firing-Squad Execution Will Be Livestreamed — but Doubts Emerge","id":"art-0034-fort-hood-firing-squad-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a judge's gavel and the scales of justice with a December calendar page, abstract and non-violent","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-firing-squad-execution-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654917349/","pinned":true,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"pentagon-livestream-firing-squad-execution-fort-hood-2026","socialHeadline":"Pentagon plans to livestream Fort Hood shooter's firing-squad execution — Vance casts doubt","sources":[{"name":"CNN — 'Hegseth vows to make first firing squad execution in decades public' (2026-10-08)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/08/politics/pete-hegseth-vows-to-make-first-firing-squad-execution-in-decades-public"},{"name":"AP/NPR — 'Pentagon says the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter will be livestreamed' (2026-10-09)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.wextradio.org/npr-news/2026-10-09/pentagon-says-the-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-will-be-livestreamed"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Fort Hood","Nidal Hasan","Pentagon","Death Penalty","Pete Hegseth"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Verified via CNN and AP/NPR page reads: Pentagon (Oct 8/9) said Dec 3, 2026 firing-squad execution of Nidal Hasan (convicted 2013, 13 murders + 32 attempted murders, 2009 Fort Hood attack) will be livestreamed; Hegseth to podcaster Jack Posobiec aboard USS Abraham Lincoln (Oct 7): 'people are able to watch it'; Acting Army Secretary Adam Telle set Dec 3, 1pm local; Trump approved; first US military execution in 60+ years, first by firing squad since WWII; survivor Alonzo Lunsford supports. IMPORTANT CAVEAT included in article: CNN Oct 10 — Army/Pentagon caught off guard, VP Vance cast doubt on whether it will happen.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["Eliud Kipchoge ended a three-year wait for a marathon victory in emphatic fashion on Sunday, winning the Melbourne Marathon in a course-record 2:09:10.","The 41-year-old Kenyan broke away from the field inside the final 10 kilometres and crossed the line two seconds inside the previous race record of 2:09:12, set by Timothy Ronoh in 2022. It was Kipchoge's 17th career marathon victory — and his first since Berlin in September 2023.","The race, which began at 6:15 a.m. local time, finished with a half-lap inside the Melbourne Cricket Ground, where Kipchoge soaked in the applause of the home crowd.","Australia's Thomas Do Canto finished second in 2:10:35, with compatriot Reece Edwards third in 2:14:33. New Zealand's Camille French won the women's race in 2:28:25. For Kipchoge, the two-time Olympic champion widely regarded as the greatest marathoner in history, the win marks a striking late-career resurgence at 41."],"breaking":false,"category":"Sports","editorPick":false,"headline":"Eliud Kipchoge, 41, Ends Three-Year Drought With Melbourne Marathon Win in Course Record","id":"art-0035-kipchoge-melbourne-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a marathon runner silhouette with a stopwatch showing 2:09:10 and a finish-line ribbon","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-kipchoge-melbourne-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"","pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"eliud-kipchoge-wins-melbourne-marathon-course-record-2026","socialHeadline":"Kipchoge wins Melbourne Marathon in course-record 2:09:10 — first win since 2023","sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Kipchoge wins first marathon in three years in Melbourne' (2026-10-11)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/kipchoge-wins-first-marathon-three-years-melbourne-2026-10-11/"},{"name":"Associated Press — Melbourne Marathon 2026 results (2026-10-11)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.europesays.com/australia/117924/"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Eliud Kipchoge","Marathon","Melbourne","Athletics","Kenya"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Verified via Reuters and AP page reads: Melbourne Marathon, Sunday Oct 11, 2026; Eliud Kipchoge (Kenya, 41) won in 2:09:10, new course record (old 2:09:12, Timothy Ronoh, 2022); 17th marathon win; first since Berlin Sep 2023; 2nd Thomas Do Canto (AUS) 2:10:35; 3rd Reece Edwards (AUS) 2:14:33; women's winner Camille French (NZL) 2:28:25; finished with half-lap inside the MCG.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"id":"art-0036-commanders-giants-ot-tie-2026","slug":"giants-commanders-27-27-overtime-tie-daniels","headline":"Commanders Botch Final Play as Clock Runs Out, Settling for 27-27 Tie With Giants","socialHeadline":"Jayden Daniels was sacked with 8 seconds left in OT and no timeouts — a 42-yard field goal never got snapped, and the Giants escaped Landover with a 27-27 tie","summary":"The Washington Commanders reached the Giants' 24-yard line in overtime and were seconds from a winning field goal — but Jayden Daniels was brought down with no timeouts left, the clock expired, and the Week 5 game ended in a 27-27 tie at Northwest Stadium. Daniels took responsibility after the game.","body":["The Washington Commanders had the win in their hands. Driving into New York Giants territory in overtime on Sunday, October 11, they stood 24 yards from the end zone, 8 seconds on the clock, and a 42-yard field goal well within Drew Stevens' range. What followed was one of the most bewildering clock-management failures of the NFL season.","Quarterback Jayden Daniels, on second-and-8 from the Giants' 24, dropped back, scrambled, and was tackled for no gain as the seconds bled away. With no timeouts remaining, the Commanders could not stop the clock or spike the ball. The officials ruled the overtime period over before Washington could run another play — and the Week 5 contest at Northwest Stadium in Landover, Maryland, finished as a 27-27 tie.","\"We have to stop the clock,\" Daniels said afterward. \"We have to know the situation. It starts with everyone, top down. Ultimately, it's on me.\" Head coach Dan Quinn refused to put the sequence on his quarterback, saying the call and the clock management were his responsibility. Quinn said the tie \"feels like a loss.\"","The ending overshadowed a dramatic game. Daniels, returning from a dislocated left elbow suffered in a Week 2 loss to Dallas, completed 17 of 25 passes for 199 yards and rushed for 103 yards and two touchdowns. Washington led 27-13 with just over seven minutes left in regulation before the Giants, behind Jameis Winston, rallied to force overtime.","The tie moved Washington to 1-3-1 on the season, ahead of a Week 6 Monday night visit to the San Francisco 49ers. The Giants stood at 3-1-1. For a league in which ties remain one of the rarest results, this one will be remembered for what happened in the final eight seconds of overtime."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Washington Commanders","New York Giants","Jayden Daniels","Overtime"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-commanders-ot-tie-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a tied 27-27 overtime scoreboard with a game clock at 0:00 over a stylized football field","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a tied 27-27 overtime scoreboard with a game clock at 0:00 over a stylized football field. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Commanders' Daniels takes blame for botched final play in OT' (Jordan Raanan, 2026-10-11)","url":"https://10bmnews.com/commanders-daniels-takes-blame-for-botched-final-play-in-ot/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Associated Press — 'Daniels, Commanders settle for tie with Giants after botching final play of OT' (via TSN, 2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.tsn.ca/nfl/article/daniels-commanders-settle-for-tie-with-giants-after-botching-final-play-of-ot/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN (Raanan) and AP page reads: Giants-Commanders 27-27 OT tie, Oct 11 2026, Northwest Stadium Landover (Week 5); Daniels tackled for no gain with 8 seconds left in OT, no timeouts, clock expired before a would-be 42-yard Drew Stevens FG; Daniels: 'Ultimately, it's on me'; Quinn took play-calling blame, tie 'feels like a loss'; Daniels returned from dislocated left elbow (Week 2), 17/25, 199 yds, 103 rushing yds, 2 TDs; records: WAS 1-3-1, NYG 3-1-1. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0037-greenlaw-ejection-49ers-seahawks-2026","slug":"greenlaw-ejected-head-butt-seahawks-32-29","headline":"Dre Greenlaw Ejected for Head-Butting Helmetless Ernest Jones IV as 49ers Edge Seahawks 32-29","socialHeadline":"The 49ers linebacker was disqualified in the second quarter after a late hit on Sam Darnold and a head-butt on a helmetless Ernest Jones IV — but San Francisco stayed unbeaten with a 32-29 win in Seattle","summary":"San Francisco stayed undefeated with a 32-29 win over Seattle on Sunday, but lost linebacker Dre Greenlaw to a second-quarter ejection after a late hit on Sam Darnold was followed by a head-butt on helmetless Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV. Seattle committed four turnovers.","body":["The San Francisco 49ers survived their own linebacker's temper on Sunday, beating the Seattle Seahawks 32-29 at Lumen Field to remain undefeated — despite losing Dre Greenlaw to an ejection midway through the second quarter.","The sequence began with a late hit by Greenlaw on Seahawks quarterback Sam Darnold near the sideline, which drew an unnecessary-roughness flag. As pushing and shoving broke out on the Seattle sideline, Greenlaw — still wearing his helmet — head-butted Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV, who was not wearing his. Officials disqualified Greenlaw from the game, ending his afternoon.","The ejection could easily have tilted the NFC West showdown toward Seattle. Instead, San Francisco's defense forced four turnovers. A fumble at the goal line recovered in the end zone by rookie defensive tackle Gracen Halton just before halftime gave the 49ers a 21-13 lead they would not surrender.","Seattle fought back: Jaxon Smith-Njigba's 16-yard touchdown put the Seahawks ahead 23-21 in the third quarter, and Jason Myers' kicking kept it close late. But the 49ers' takeaways proved decisive in the 32-29 final.","Greenlaw's ejection adds to a heated chapter of the 49ers-Seahawks rivalry. No suspension had been announced as of publication, and this story makes no claim about further league discipline."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","San Francisco 49ers","Seattle Seahawks","Dre Greenlaw","Ejection"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-greenlaw-ejection-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of two stylized football helmets colliding, a referee penalty flag and a red ejection whistle motif","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of two stylized football helmets colliding, a referee penalty flag and a red ejection whistle motif. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — '49ers capitalize on four turnovers to down Seahawks, remain undefeated' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/nfl/49ers-capitalize-four-turnovers-down-seahawks-remain-undefeated--flm-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Sporting News — 'Why Dre Greenlaw was ejected from Seahawks-49ers' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.sportingnews.com/us/nfl/news/dre-greenlaw-ejected-seahawks-49ers-confrontation-ernest-jones/ddd16b3af9c431af7e947309","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via Reuters game report and Sporting News page reads: 49ers beat Seahawks 32-29 in Seattle, Oct 11 2026 (Week 5); Greenlaw ejected in 2nd quarter after late hit on Darnold near sideline, then head-butted helmetless LB Ernest Jones IV; Seattle committed 4 turnovers; 49ers remain undefeated; Halton goal-line fumble recovery TD before halftime. Suspension speculation unconfirmed — story makes no suspension claim. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0038-packers-bears-burden-quit-2026","slug":"packers-beat-bears-31-7-burden-quit","headline":"Packers Maul Bears 31-7, Then Fire Back at Luther Burden III: 'He Quit'","socialHeadline":"Green Bay backed up its pregame talk with a 31-7 rout at Lambeau, then answered Bears receiver Luther Burden III's 'make them quit' vow — as Chicago played without injured Caleb Williams","summary":"The Green Bay Packers thrashed the Chicago Bears 31-7 at Lambeau Field on Sunday, then delivered the verbal knockout. Linebacker Zaire Franklin fired back at Bears receiver Luther Burden III, who had promised before the game to 'beat them real bad and make them quit' — 'He quit today,' Franklin said. Chicago played without injured quarterback Caleb Williams.","body":["The talking started before kickoff. Chicago Bears receiver Luther Burden III vowed his team would \"beat them real bad and make them quit\" when the Bears visited Lambeau Field on Sunday. The Green Bay Packers heard it — and made the trash talk their motivation in a 31-7 Week 5 rout on October 11, 2026.","After the game, Packers linebacker Zaire Franklin delivered the rebuttal. \"He quit today,\" Franklin said of Burden, turning the receiver's own vow back on him after Green Bay dominated in all phases.","The Bears were also shorthanded where it mattered most. With starting quarterback Caleb Williams injured, Chicago turned to backup Tyson Bagent, and the offense never found its rhythm against a Packers defense that fed off the home crowd.","The 31-7 final was a statement in the NFC North's oldest rivalry — and a reminder that pregame guarantees only count if you back them up. Burden and the Bears learned that lesson the hard way at Lambeau."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Green Bay Packers","Chicago Bears","Luther Burden","Rivalry"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-packers-bears-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a 31-7 final score with Week 5 tag, green-gold and navy-orange bars and a stylized football","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a 31-7 final score with Week 5 tag, green-gold and navy-orange bars and a stylized football. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Packers maul Bears, fire back at Burden quit talk' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.espn.ph/nfl/story/_/id/50162146/packers-maul-bears-fire-back-burden-quit-talk","role":"primary"},{"name":"NBC Sports — 'Packers LB Zaire Franklin: Luther Burden said he'd make us quit, but he quit Sunday' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/packers-lb-zaire-franklin-luther-burden-said-hed-make-us-quit-but-he-quit-sunday","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN and NBC Sports page reads: Packers beat Bears 31-7 at Lambeau, Week 5, Oct 11 2026; LB Zaire Franklin's 'He quit today' response to WR Luther Burden III's pregame 'beat them real bad and make them quit' vow; Bears started Tyson Bagent for injured Caleb Williams. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0039-big-ten-oregon-ucla-spot-2026","slug":"big-ten-admits-error-oregon-ucla-2-point-conversion","headline":"Big Ten Admits Officials Spotted Ball Wrong on Oregon's Do-or-Die 2-Point Try in 17-15 Loss to UCLA","socialHeadline":"The conference said the ball should have been spotted at the half-yard line — not the 1.5-yard line — for Oregon's tying attempt with 2:16 left. The Ducks were stuffed, and UCLA held on to win at Autzen.","summary":"The Big Ten admitted on Sunday that officials incorrectly spotted the ball on Oregon's tying 2-point conversion attempt with 2:16 left in a 17-15 loss to UCLA at Autzen Stadium. The ball was placed at the 1.5-yard line instead of the half-yard line after a UCLA facemask penalty — and the Ducks were stopped short.","body":["One yard. That was the difference the Big Ten admitted to on Sunday, October 11, a day after the Oregon Ducks fell 17-15 to the UCLA Bruins at Autzen Stadium.","With 2:16 left in the fourth quarter, Oregon quarterback Brock Thomas ran up the middle on a first 2-point try and was stopped — but UCLA linebacker Sammy Omosigho grabbed his facemask, drawing a personal foul. The penalty should have moved the ball half the distance to the goal from the end of the run: the half-yard line. Instead, officials spotted it from the original line of scrimmage, placing it at the 1.5-yard line.","In a statement released through ESPN's Pete Thamel, the conference confirmed the error. The ball should have been spotted, in the conference's words, half the distance to the goal from the end of the run of the first attempt — not from where the play started.","Given the second chance from the 1.5-yard line, Oregon handed to running back Jordon Davison, who was stuffed by defensive tackle Tyson Ford short of the goal line. The Ducks' last-gasp lateral play on the final snap ended with a fumble recovered by UCLA's Dante Lovett.","The Bruins improved to 5-0 and climbed to No. 12 in the Associated Press rankings, while Oregon fell to 3-2 — its second loss of the season. Whether the misplaced spot changed the outcome will be debated all week; the admission itself, rare for the conference, is already fueling the argument."],"category":"Sports","tags":["College Football","Oregon Ducks","UCLA Bruins","Big Ten","Officiating"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-big-ten-spot-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a football under a magnifying glass at the half-yard line with 2:16 remaining on a 2-point conversion","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a football under a magnifying glass at the half-yard line with 2:16 remaining on a 2-point conversion. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Sports Illustrated — 'Big Ten Admits Officiating Mistake in Crucial Play of Oregon's Loss to UCLA Bruins' (2026-10-11, quoting full Big Ten statement via ESPN's Pete Thamel)","url":"https://www.si.com/college/oregon/football/big-ten-admits-officiating-mistake-crucial-play-oregon-ducks-loss-ucla-bruins","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today — 'Big Ten releases statement on critical officiating mistake in Oregon-UCLA' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://duckswire.usatoday.com/story/sports/college/ducks/football/2026/10/11/oregon-football-big-ten-makes-statement-officiating-mistake-ucla/92209464007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via SI (quoting full Big Ten statement) and USA Today page reads: UCLA beat Oregon 17-15 at Autzen, Oct 10 2026; Big Ten admitted Oct 11 that officials spotted ball at 1.5-yard line instead of half-yard line for Oregon's 2nd 2-point attempt with 2:16 left, after UCLA facemask on Brock Thomas (Omosigho) on first attempt; Jordon Davison stuffed by Tyson Ford on retry; UCLA first win at Autzen since 2004, 5-0 / AP No. 12; Oregon 3-2, second loss. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0040-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-2026","slug":"fernando-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-patriots","headline":"No. 1 Pick Fernando Mendoza Makes NFL Debut in Raiders' 45-17 Loss to Patriots","socialHeadline":"The 2026 top draft pick entered late at Gillette Stadium, going 6-of-8 for 48 yards in mop-up duty. Coach Klint Kubiak: 'He did a good job.'","summary":"The 2026 No. 1 overall pick is officially an NFL quarterback. Fernando Mendoza made his regular-season debut for the Las Vegas Raiders on Sunday, entering late in a 45-17 loss to the New England Patriots at Gillette Stadium. The rookie completed 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards, and coach Klint Kubiak praised his first outing.","body":["It came in garbage time, but it was history. With about six minutes left on Sunday and the Las Vegas Raiders trailing the New England Patriots 45-17 at Gillette Stadium, the 2026 No. 1 overall pick jogged onto the field for his first NFL regular-season action.","Fernando Mendoza, the Raiders' franchise hope from the 2026 draft, operated the offense calmly in his brief stint, completing 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards against a Patriots defense protecting a 28-point lead.","Head coach Klint Kubiak liked what he saw. \"He did a good job,\" Kubiak said of the rookie's first taste of NFL speed.","The result itself was never in doubt — the Patriots controlled the Week 5 game throughout on October 11. But for Raiders fans, the scoreline was secondary. The debut of the No. 1 pick, however brief, was the moment that mattered, and Mendoza now has his first NFL snaps in the books."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Las Vegas Raiders","New England Patriots","Fernando Mendoza","NFL Draft"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-mendoza-debut-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a stylized quarterback silhouette with No. 1 pick and NFL debut motifs","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a stylized quarterback silhouette with No. 1 pick and NFL debut motifs. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Raiders QB Fernando Mendoza makes NFL regular-season debut in late loss to Patriots' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.espn.ph/nfl/story/_/id/50161581/raiders-qb-fernando-mendoza-makes-nfl-regular-season-debut-late-loss-patriots","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today — 'Fernando Mendoza Raiders NFL debut' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/patriots/2026/10/11/fernando-mendoza-raiders-nfl-debut/92207222007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN and USA Today page reads: 2026 No. 1 overall pick Fernando Mendoza debuted for Raiders late in 45-17 loss to Patriots at Gillette Stadium, Week 5, Oct 11 2026; entered with ~6:00 left down 28; 6-of-8, 48 yards; coach Klint Kubiak: 'He did a good job.' No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0041-asia-markets-earnings-oil-2026","slug":"asia-shares-cautious-earnings-season-oil-slips","headline":"Asian Shares Open Cautiously as Earnings Season Looms and Oil Slips","socialHeadline":"Investors stayed on the sidelines Monday ahead of the US earnings season, with South Korea down 1.1% and crude sliding on confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire claim and Gulf strikes","summary":"Asian shares started Monday cautiously as investors braced for the US earnings season, which kicks off with the big banks on Tuesday. South Korea fell 1.1%, while oil slid — Brent down 1.1% to $103.50 and US crude 1.2% lower at $90.73 — amid confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire announcement and strikes in the Gulf.","body":["Asian markets opened the week on a cautious note on Monday, October 12, with investors holding back ahead of the US third-quarter earnings season. America's biggest banks report on Tuesday, setting the tone for a reporting season Wall Street will read closely for signs of how the economy is weathering the autumn.","South Korea was among the region's weakest performers, dropping 1.1% as the defensive mood spread across the region's trading floors.","Energy markets added to the uncertainty. Brent crude slipped 1.1% to $103.50 a barrel and US crude fell 1.2% to $90.73, as traders weighed confusion over an unconfirmed energy-ceasefire announcement by US President Donald Trump against reports of continued strikes in the Gulf.","With earnings, energy headlines, and geopolitics all pulling in different directions, Monday's session set up a week where Asian markets will take their cues from Wall Street's results as much as from their own fundamentals."],"category":"Business","tags":["Markets","Asia","Stocks","Oil","Earnings"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-asia-markets-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of candlestick stock charts, an Asia map outline and an oil barrel with a downward arrow","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of candlestick stock charts, an Asia map outline and an oil barrel with a downward arrow. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Global markets: Shares cautious in Asia as earnings loom, oil slips' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/china/global-markets-wrapup-1-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Devdiscourse — 'Global Markets: Shares cautious in Asia as earnings loom, oil slips' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/international/3990565-global-markets-shares-cautious-in-asia-as-earnings-loom-oil-slips","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via Reuters wire and Devdiscourse page reads: Asian shares cautious Monday Oct 12 ahead of US earnings season (banks Tuesday); South Korea -1.1%; Brent -1.1% to $103.50, US crude -1.2% to $90.73, on confusion over Trump's unconfirmed energy-ceasefire claim and Gulf strikes. Ephemeral daily wire. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0042-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-game1-2026","slug":"brewers-edge-dodgers-2-1-nlcs-game-1-turang-homer","headline":"Brewers Edge Dodgers 2-1 in NLCS Game 1 Behind Turang Homer and Shutdown Bullpen","socialHeadline":"Turang's 4th-inning homer and 4 2/3 scoreless bullpen innings gave Milwaukee a 2-1 NLCS Game 1 win over the Dodgers","summary":"The Milwaukee Brewers took Game 1 of the National League Championship Series 2-1 over the Los Angeles Dodgers on October 11, riding Brice Turang's tying home run, rookie Luis Lara's go-ahead single and 4 2/3 scoreless innings from their bullpen at American Family Field.","body":["The Milwaukee Brewers drew first blood in the National League Championship Series on Saturday, October 11, 2026, defeating the Los Angeles Dodgers 2-1 in Game 1 at American Family Field. It was the first NLCS meeting of two 100-win teams since the 1976 Reds and Phillies, and it lived up to the billing as a pitchers' duel.","Brice Turang provided the first breakthrough, launching a 384-foot home run to left-center off Tarik Skubal in the fourth inning to erase a 1-0 deficit. An inning later, rookie Luis Lara delivered the decisive blow: with Garrett Mitchell aboard after a walk and moved up on Cooper Pratt's sacrifice bunt, Lara lined a tiebreaking RBI single off Skubal to put Milwaukee ahead 2-1.","The Brewers' bullpen made the slim lead stand up. D.L. Hall, Abner Uribe, Aaron Ashby and Trevor Megill combined for 4 2/3 scoreless innings, with Megill surviving two ninth-inning walks to earn the save when Mookie Betts flied out to end it. The victory snapped Milwaukee's seven-game postseason losing streak against the Dodgers, who swept them in last year's NLCS.","Skubal, the two-time AL Cy Young winner acquired from Detroit at the trade deadline, took the loss despite striking out seven over five innings, allowing two runs on five hits with two walks. It was only his second defeat in eight career postseason starts. The Dodgers' lone run came on Andy Pages' second-inning RBI single that scored Shohei Ohtani; Los Angeles went 1-for-6 with runners in scoring position, grounded into three double plays and stranded nine runners.","A crowd of 42,617 watched the opener. Game 2 is set for Monday, October 12, in Milwaukee, with Yoshinobu Yamamoto scheduled for the Dodgers against Logan Henderson for the Brewers."],"category":"Sports","tags":["MLB","NLCS","Milwaukee Brewers","Los Angeles Dodgers","Brice Turang"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated scoreboard showing Brewers 2, Dodgers 1 in NLCS Game 1","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated scoreboard showing Brewers 2, Dodgers 1 in NLCS Game 1. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — Brewers 2, Dodgers 1, NLCS Game 1 (2026-10-11)","url":"https://apnews.com/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — NLCS Game 1 report (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP game story as primary; Reuters and Sportradar box-score data corroborate score, scorers, pitching lines and Game 2 matchup. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0043-ravens-falcons-ot-2026","slug":"ravens-beat-falcons-30-23-ot-huntley-penix-injured","headline":"Huntley Stars as Ravens Stun Falcons 30-23 in Overtime; Penix Exits With Rib Injury","socialHeadline":"Backup QB Tyler Huntley threw for 201 yards and 2 TDs and ran in the OT winner as Baltimore beat Atlanta 30-23; Michael Penix Jr. left late with a rib injury","summary":"The Baltimore Ravens beat the Atlanta Falcons 30-23 in overtime on Sunday night, October 11, as backup quarterback Tyler Huntley threw for 201 yards and two touchdowns and scored the winning touchdown on a 1-yard run. Falcons starter Michael Penix Jr. left the game late in regulation with a rib injury.","body":["The Baltimore Ravens needed overtime and their backup quarterback to escape Atlanta with a 30-23 victory over the Falcons on Sunday night, October 11, 2026, at Mercedes-Benz Stadium. Tyler Huntley, starting in place of the injured Lamar Jackson (ankle), completed 24 of 32 passes for 201 yards and two touchdowns, then capped the opening drive of overtime with a 1-yard touchdown run with 2:57 remaining.","The comeback began with Baltimore trailing 23-15 and only 2:25 left in regulation. Huntley engineered a six-play, 71-yard drive, finding Devontez Walker for a 7-yard touchdown with 40 seconds left before Derrick Henry took a direct snap for the tying two-point conversion. In overtime, safety Kyle Hamilton intercepted Falcons backup Tua Tagovailoa to seal the win.","The Falcons lost more than the game. Starting quarterback Michael Penix Jr. was sacked by Tavius Robinson with 27 seconds left in a tie game and suffered a rib injury. Penix walked off under his own power and was listed as questionable; he briefly re-entered for one play, which fell incomplete, then watched overtime from the sideline with a towel over his head as Tagovailoa finished the game in his Falcons debut. Penix finished 19 of 32 for 240 yards and a touchdown and said afterward he does not expect the injury to be a long-term issue and hopes to play next week.","Derrick Henry powered the Ravens with 102 rushing yards plus an 18-yard touchdown reception, while Drake London caught seven passes for 118 yards for Atlanta. Jessie Bates III returned a fumble 36 yards for a Falcons touchdown in the first quarter. Ravens coach Jesse Minter publicly praised Huntley's performance after the game.","The win moved Baltimore to 4-1 and into sole possession of first place in the AFC North. Atlanta fell to 2-3."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Baltimore Ravens","Atlanta Falcons","Tyler Huntley","Michael Penix Jr."],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-ravens-falcons-ot-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated scoreboard showing Ravens 30, Falcons 23 in overtime","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated scoreboard showing Ravens 30, Falcons 23 in overtime. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — Ravens 30, Falcons 23 OT game story (2026-10-11)","url":"https://apnews.com/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Ravens-Falcons Week 5 report (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"NBC Sports — Ravens-Falcons coverage (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP game story as primary; Reuters and NBC Sports corroborate score, stats, injury sequence and standings. Penix long-term outlook is his own attributed statement, not a medical fact. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0044-trump-energy-ceasefire-2026","slug":"trump-claims-energy-ceasefire-ukraine-russia-oil-falls","headline":"Trump Claims Ukraine-Russia 'Energy Ceasefire' Agreed; Oil Prices Fall as Neither Side Confirms","socialHeadline":"Trump announced an 'energy ceasefire' on Truth Social; oil fell Monday, but Ukraine said it was awaiting details and Russia has not commented","summary":"US President Donald Trump announced on Sunday, October 11, that Ukraine and Russia had agreed to an immediate \"energy ceasefire.\" Oil prices fell on Monday, but neither Kyiv nor Moscow confirmed any agreement, with Ukraine's president saying the announcement was news to him.","body":["US President Donald Trump declared on his Truth Social platform on Sunday, October 11, 2026, that Ukraine and Russia had agreed to an immediate halt to strikes on energy infrastructure. \"Effective immediately, there is an ENERGY CEASEFIRE in the War between Russia and Ukraine. Both parties have agreed. Do not break it!\" he wrote, according to reporting by CNN.","Oil markets reacted on Monday: Brent crude fell $1.54, or 1.47%, to $103.18 a barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate dropped 1.68% to $90.31 and ICE gasoil slipped 3% to $1,436, Reuters reported. But the supposed agreement itself remained unverified. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy told Axios the announcement was \"news for me,\" and later posted that Ukraine supports a ceasefire but is \"awaiting details from the American side.\" Russia has not commented at all.","The announcement came days after a controversial diesel arrangement under which Russia is to immediately supply more than 300,000 metric tons (2.25 million barrels) of diesel, followed by 500,000 tons in November and one million tons afterward, with temporary US sanctions relief, according to Fox News and CNN reporting. IEA chief Fatih Birol on Sunday urged member countries to assess possible diesel releases.","Analysts urged caution. \"Questions remain over the validity and longevity of any such ceasefire... without clearer evidence that it will actually hold, the extent of the pullback is likely to stay limited,\" analyst Tim Waterer said, as quoted by Reuters. The continuing Middle East conflict is meanwhile keeping Brent above $100 a barrel.","NewsVeria notes: as of publication, the \"energy ceasefire\" exists only as a claim by President Trump. No confirmation has come from Ukraine or Russia, and readers should treat it as unconfirmed until independently verified by the parties involved."],"category":"World","tags":["Donald Trump","Ukraine","Russia","Oil Prices","Energy"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-energy-ceasefire-oil-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated oil barrels with a falling price arrow","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated oil barrels with a falling price arrow. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Donald Trump — Truth Social post (2026-10-11), via CNN","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/11/politics/trump-ukraine-russia-energy-ceasefire","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — oil market report (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/markets/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Trump's Truth Social post (quoted by CNN) is the primary source for the announcement; Reuters market data corroborates the oil-price move. Framing is mandatory: presented strictly as an unconfirmed claim — neither Ukraine nor Russia has confirmed any agreement. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0045-saudi-travel-warnings-2026","slug":"travel-warnings-saudi-arabia-houthi-airport-attacks","headline":"Seven Countries Issue Travel Warnings for Saudi Arabia After Houthi Airport Attacks","socialHeadline":"The US, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand advised against travel to parts of Saudi Arabia after a wave of attacks on Saudi airports","summary":"Seven countries — the United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand — have issued travel advisories against Saudi Arabia following a series of Houthi attacks on Saudi airports, including strikes that closed major airports and killed more than a dozen people, according to Saudi authorities.","body":["Governments around the world moved on Sunday and Monday to warn their citizens against travel to Saudi Arabia after a wave of attacks on the kingdom's airports claimed by Yemen's Houthi movement. The United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand all issued or updated advisories, Al Jazeera reported.","The advisories vary in scope. Australia's Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade told citizens to avoid Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport and reconsider travel to other Saudi airports. New Zealand advised against all travel to the Riyadh airport and the Najran, Jazan and Asir provinces. The US Embassy in Riyadh on Sunday advised Americans to reconsider travel, citing Iranian and Houthi threats. Canada advised against non-essential travel to any part of Saudi Arabia, South Korea urged citizens to leave unless on essential business, and Britain advised against travel to Jeddah and Dammam and all airports except Medina's except for essential reasons.","The warnings follow five attacks on Saudi airports in under a week. King Khalid and King Fahd international airports were closed. The Houthis claimed the four strikes before Sunday's, which went unclaimed. Saudi Arabia's civil aviation authority said Sunday's attack killed one person and injured 11. For Saturday's attack, Saudi authorities reported 12 dead and more than 300 wounded, according to Reuters; Al Jazeera reported 13 killed, a small discrepancy between outlets. The dead included four Saudis and two Bangladeshis, plus American, Jordanian, Palestinian, Syrian, Sudanese and Egyptian nationals, according to Saudi authorities via Reuters.","Reuters separately reported that Yemen's Houthis renewed their warning over Saudi airports after the deadly Riyadh attack, signalling the threat to aviation remains active."],"category":"World","tags":["Saudi Arabia","Houthis","Travel Advisory","Yemen","Aviation"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-saudi-travel-warning-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated airplane over a desert airport with a warning sign","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated airplane over a desert airport with a warning sign. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Government travel advisories — US State Dept, UK FCDO, Australia DFAT, NZ MFAT, Global Affairs Canada, ROK MFA (2026-10-11/12), via Al Jazeera","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/10/12/countries-warn-against-travel-to-saudi-arabia-following-houthi-attacks","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Houthis renew warning over Saudi airports (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/yemens-houthis-renew-warning-over-saudi-airports-after-deadly-riyadh-attack-2026-10-11/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: the government advisories themselves (quoted via Al Jazeera's roundup); corroboration: Reuters on the attacks and 